      "text": "To find the value of \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor\\), we need to evaluate the floor function for each integer part of the square roots of the numbers from 1 to 16. The floor function \\(\\lfloor x \\rfloor\\) returns the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\nHere are the values we need to find:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor &= 1, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor &= 1, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor &= 1, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{4} \\rfloor &= 2, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{5} \\rfloor &= 2, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{6} \\rfloor &= 2, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{7} \\rfloor &= 2, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{8} \\rfloor &= 2, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{13} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{14} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{15} \\rfloor &= 3, \\\\\n\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor &= 4.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum these values:\n\\[\n1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 4.\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\\[\n1 + 1 + 1 = 3,\n\\]\n\\[\n3 + 2 = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\n5 + 2 = 7,\n\\]\n\\[\n7 + 2 = 9,\n\\]\n\\[\n9 + 3 = 12,\n\\]\n\\[\n12 + 3 = 15,\n\\]\n\\[\n15 + 3 = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\n18 + 3 = 21,\n\\]\n\\[\n21 + 3 = 24,\n\\]\n\\[\n24 + 4 = 28.\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum is \\(\\boxed{28}\\).",
